PSC case 26-E-0045 is a new state proceeding on how large power users connect to the grid. The event body is empty and lists no impacts, and it contains no instructions. Nothing on file ties it to our live approvals. The NYSEG settings acceptance (to_accept) and the witness and energization (witness) appear to be governed by the existing interconnection, but we have not confirmed that.

The risk is a policy change, a moratorium or new conditions that reach energization. With only 3 business days of float on the critical path (to_accept, witness, l3, l4) and 5 holiday days already eating into it, any regulatory pause would push L4 past the 2027-02-22 lease date.

No date changes from this event. My response is low-cost and needs no new commitments:
- confirm exposure through the lessee, since we have no direct line to TeraWulf or NYSEG;
- brief our team;
- have counsel check that colocation rights are preserved if new conditions emerge;
- ask through the lessee whether TeraWulf can get NYSEG to book the witness test promptly after acceptance, to claw back float against the holidays.

